Egypt in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (pharaoh in the double crown, pyramids and sphinx, seated colossi, lighthouse, domes and minarets, canal and steamer,
dam and pylons, Cairo skyline and tower, feluccas) are original stylised silhouettes drawn as simple paths,
not traced from photographs. No logos, no flags, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): a harp by physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, Lemo-Opuscar, MIT);
sistrum, frame drum and ney flute synthesised in code. No samples.
Sound (mix.py): paper swish, stamps, wind, birds, river, waves, gulls, a steamer horn, turbine rush, city hum: synthesised in code.
Mastering: FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) via imageio-ffmpeg.

Facts and sources: FACTS.md.
